00:16:58.993 --> 00:17:08.465
Dedupe at intake: a unique constraint on the producer's dedupe key (insert... on conflict do nothing) absorbs redelivered events (Ch 20).

262
00:17:08.745 --> 00:17:13.950
Leases, not locks: workers claim jobs with FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED and a short lease.

263
00:17:14.230 --> 00:17:18.198
A crashed worker's jobs become claimable again, so nothing is lost.

264
00:17:19.548 --> 00:17:24.540
Unknown outcomes: a timeout or a crash after sending leaves the outcome unknown.

265
00:17:24.820 --> 00:17:28.319
Retrying risks a duplicate; not retrying risks a loss.

266
00:17:28.599 --> 00:17:39.905
Only an idempotency key the vendor honours (a client reference the vendor dedupes on, or FCM's message id semantics, VERIFY each vendor's guarantee) closes the gap.

267
00:17:40.185 --> 00:17:42.980
Where the vendor can't dedupe, choose per message class.

268
00:17:43.260 --> 00:18:00.327
Refunds and payments: prefer a rare duplicate with idempotent wording (Your refund of 1,240 rupeesfor order 88213 is processed is harmless twice; You have received 1,240 rupees is not).

