00:28:46.681 --> 00:29:02.105
OTPs behind a campaign in one FIFO queue; duplicate refund SMS; a silent vendor failure undetected for 45 min; promotional SMS after 21:00; notification fatigue and uninstalls.

435
00:29:02.385 --> 00:29:22.268
Decision, Message classes with separate lanes and a separate promotional route; dedupe keys at intake, leased jobs, vendor idempotency keys; DLR-health vendor routing with OTP resend; a policy engine for consent, quiet hours, caps, collapse and push-first escalation; DLT-bound templates.

436
00:29:23.618 --> 00:29:48.045
Related ADRs, ADR-260 Four message classes and per-class lanes or pools; promotional traffic on its own vendor route (L1); ADR-261 Producer-supplied dedupe keys, unique at intake; SKIP LOCKED leases; vendor client references (L2); ADR-262 DLR-health routing per vendor and operator, 85% threshold,

437
00:29:48.325 --> 00:30:20.318
5% probe; OTP resend via alternate vendor at 20 s (L3); ADR-263 Policy engine: consent per channel and purpose, quiet hours, promo cap 2 per day, collapse keys, daily digest, push-first with 60 s SMS escalation (L4); ADR-264 Templates versioned with DLT ids, rendering tested in CI; ADR-265 Message log 90 days hot, then aggregated.

