442
00:30:39.449 --> 00:30:43.887
R4 No promotional message outside consent or legal windows.

443
00:30:44.167 --> 00:30:50.311
R5 SMS spend reduced ≥ 50% without reducing critical reach.

444
00:30:50.591 --> 00:30:51.999
Decisions in detail.

445
00:30:53.349 --> 00:30:55.589
Lanes (ADR-260).

446
00:30:55.869 --> 00:31:06.621
Kafka topics per class; worker pools per class; SMS egress shaped per class with OTP strict priority; promotional route 400 SMS per second.

447
00:31:06.901 --> 00:31:22.410
Delivery (ADR-261). notificationrequest.dedupekey unique; job leases 30 s (300 ms in the lab); max 8 attempts, then DLQ with alert; vendor client reference = message id.

448
00:31:22.690 --> 00:31:25.101
Routing (ADR-262).

449
00:31:25.381 --> 00:31:34.597
Health per vendor times operator from DLRs, 60 s window; cheapest healthy vendor; OTP resend if no DLR by 20 s.

450
00:31:34.877 --> 00:31:37.437
Policy (ADR-263).

451
00:31:37.717 --> 00:31:44.821
Preferences cached per user; counters in Redis; collapse per order; digests at 19:00 local.

452
00:31:46.171 --> 00:31:48.645
Templates (ADR-264).

453
00:31:48.925 --> 00:31:53.939
Template registry with DLT header or template ids, languages and owners.

454
00:31:54.219 --> 00:31:55.243
Consequences.

455
00:31:55.523 --> 00:32:01.795
More moving parts (policy engine, router, tracker), and dependence on vendor DLR quality.

456
00:32:02.075 --> 00:32:06.043
Collapsing and escalation add a little latency to some messages.

457
00:32:06.323 --> 00:32:07.261
In return:

458
00:32:07.541 --> 00:32:16.437
OTPs that arrive during campaigns, no double refunds, fast detection of vendor failures, and less than a quarter of the SMS spend.

