00:48:05.070 --> 00:48:06.734
Caps, collapse, digests.

636
00:48:08.084 --> 00:48:09.172
Observability.

637
00:48:09.452 --> 00:48:14.103
End-to-end latency per class (requested, then delivered), per channel and vendor.

638
00:48:14.383 --> 00:48:21.060
DLR delivery rate per vendor times operator times circle, with thresholds that drive routing and alerts.

639
00:48:21.340 --> 00:48:24.647
Queue depth and age per lane; OTP expiry rate.

640
00:48:24.927 --> 00:48:30.324
Duplicate rate (same dedupe key delivered twice, from DLRs) and DLQ size.

641
00:48:30.604 --> 00:48:37.580
Suppression reasons (opted out, capped, collapsed, quiet hours), a sudden change usually means a policy bug.

642
00:48:38.930 --> 00:48:40.359
Spend per class per day.

643
00:48:41.709 --> 00:48:43.267
Security and privacy.

644
00:48:43.547 --> 00:48:49.755
Minimise content: masked identifiers, no full addresses or amounts beyond need in SMS.

645
00:48:50.035 --> 00:48:58.504
OTP messages carry app-hash or domain-bound formats for autofill and anti-phishing (Android SMS Retriever, WebOTP).

646
00:48:58.784 --> 00:49:02.731
Vendor webhooks authenticated (signatures, allow-listed IPs).

647
00:49:03.011 --> 00:49:09.240
Consent records and message logs are personal data: retention and erasure (Ch 36).

648
00:49:10.590 --> 00:49:11.486
Performance.

649
00:49:11.766 --> 00:49:21.579
Batch push sends (FCM batch APIs), connection reuse to vendors, async I or O or virtual threads for vendor calls (Ch 19).

650
00:49:21.859 --> 00:49:26.169
Keep the job table small: move finished messages to the log partition.

651
00:49:26.449 --> 00:49:32.401
Policy evaluation from cached preferences and Redis counters, not per-message database reads.

652
00:49:33.751 --> 00:49:34.476
Cost.

653
00:49:34.756 --> 00:49:42.969
SMS dominates: routing to the cheapest healthy vendor (L3) and push-first escalation (L4) are the biggest levers.

654
00:49:43.249 --> 00:49:47.793
WhatsApp and email have different pricing; choose channels per class and region.

655
00:49:48.073 --> 00:49:55.028
Report spend per class and per campaign; charge back campaign sends to marketing budgets (Ch 35).

